    "description": "In this video, Chef John shows you how to make Czech bread dumplings, or knedliky. The recipe is easy to follow and uses a simple dough made with warm milk, sugar, dry active yeast, an egg, salt, and Wondra Flour. The dough is kneaded until it is smooth and elastic, then left to rise for two hours. Once it has doubled in size, the dough is shaped into a tube and left to proof for 20 to 25 minutes. The dumplings are then boiled and can be served with gravy or other sauces. Chef John notes that these dumplings are particularly good at soaking up gravy and are a comforting addition to any meal.",
